-- The power armor, ground vehicles and aircraft from Rifts World Book Ten:
-- Juicer Uprising, printed 77-88. Seven rows, and the last of the book.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-juicer-uprising-gear-c.sql
--
-- The book has a TEXT LAYER, so this was read with scripts/read-columns.py and
-- transcribed rather than OCR'd. The printed-to-PDF offset is ZERO.
--
-- THIRD AND LAST GEAR BATCH, and the worst-fitting data in the book. A Rifts
-- vehicle is not one row of numbers: it is a Model Type, a Class, a Crew, an
-- M.D.C. BY LOCATION table, a Speed block with separate running, flying and
-- leaping figures, a Statistical Data block, and a numbered list of weapon
-- systems each with its own damage, rate of fire, range and payload.
--
-- The gear table has no location column and no weapon-system table, and this
-- import does NOT add either. It follows the eleven vehicle rows already in the
-- catalog: `mdc` holds the MAIN BODY figure, `cost` and `weight_lbs` hold theirs,
-- `damage` summarises the weapon systems, `range` carries the speed block, and
-- the whole stat block goes into `description` as prose. That is how
-- northern-gun-sky-king, the-big-boss-a-t-v and a-t-v-speedster-hover-cycle are
-- already stored, and a vehicle that reads differently from the ones beside it
-- would be worse than one that is merely verbose.
--
-- SEVEN ROWS, NOT EIGHT. The NG-JK1A and the NG-JK1B are one entry in the book,
-- with the B model's figures in parentheses throughout, so they are one row -
-- main body 170 with the B's 210 in the description, and both prices in
-- cost_note. Same call as the Forearm Vibro-Blades' double and tri configurations
-- in gear batch A.
--
-- The Road Boss stores its UNARMED price of 90,000 rather than the 200,000 it
-- costs with full weapon systems, because the weapons are the option and the
-- vehicle is the thing; both figures are in cost_note. Every other row here
-- prices the vehicle as sold.
--
-- TWO OF THESE ARE WHY TWO OF THIS BOOK'S SKILLS EXIST. Piloting: Jump Bike
-- Combat is written for the Tarantula and Piloting: Flight System Combat for the
-- Icarus; both skills were imported in add-juicer-uprising-skills.sql, or rather
-- found already present from RUE. The rows say so, so the connection is visible
-- from either end.
--
-- Pure ASCII with LF line endings, comments included, per PR #93 and #101.
-- ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING, not DO UPDATE: every row here is new, and
-- nothing in this file should ever overwrite a curated value.

INSERT INTO gear (slug, name, system, category, weight_lbs, cost, cost_note, damage, is_mega_damage,
                  range, payload, mdc, description, source_book) VALUES
('ng-jk1-juicer-killer-power-armor', 'NG-JK1A/B "Juicer Killer" Power Armor', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 250.0, 3600000, 'Market cost 3.6 million credits for a new JK1A; the JK1B is 4.4 million. Drop 2 million credits if the targeting computer is not included.', 'Laser guns (2): 3D6 M.D. per blast, 6D6 M.D. for a double blast at one target, range 4,000 feet (1,220 m), effectively unlimited payload. Particle beam guns (2), forearm mini-rail guns (2) and chest grenade launchers (4) as well. Hand to hand: restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full strength 1D6 M.D., power punch 2D6 M.D., kick 1D6 M.D.', 1, 'Running 90 mph (144.8 kmph) maximum, tiring the operator at 10% of the usual rate. JK1A cannot fly; the JK1B has upper-back thrusters (70 M.D.C.) for five-minute bursts at up to 100 mph (160 kmph) and 300 feet (91.5 m). Unassisted leap 25 feet (7.6 m) up or 30 feet (9.1 m) across; a booster-assisted leap carries 100 feet (30.5 m) in any direction.', 'Nuclear; average energy life 15 years', 170, 'Model Type NG-JK1, models A and B - the B is 10% larger with more armor and limited flight. Class: Light Assault Exoskeleton. Crew: one. A very light scout power armor married to an advanced reflex response system and a targeting computer tied to FOUR energy weapons THAT OPERATE INDEPENDENTLY OF THE WEARER. The computer is built to follow, respond to and even predict the movements of Juicers and other super-fast beings and lead them enough to hit: a Juicer facing one LOSES HIS AUTOMATIC DODGE against its special attacks and must take evasive action. One on one it is like fighting three opponents - the computer with two weapon pairs and EIGHT attacks per melee, plus the pilot acting independently. M.D.C. by location, JK1B figures in parentheses: main body 170 (210), head 60 (75), arms 90 each (120), legs 100 each (130), chest plates and grenade launchers 90 each (120), laser guns 25 each (30), particle beam guns 30 each (40), forearm mini-rail guns 40 each (60), computer and sensor cluster 80 (90). Destroying the head costs all optics and sensors, all power armor combat bonuses, and drops the computer from eight attacks to six; a called shot at -4. DESTROYING THE COMPUTER nullifies every anti-Juicer advantage and drops its attacks to ZERO - the pilot must then work the four guns himself, each use costing one of his own attacks; also a called shot at -4. Depleting the main body shuts the suit down entirely. Height 7 feet (2.4 m), width 4.5 feet (1.37 m), length 4 feet (1.2 m). Physical strength equal to P.S. 30. No cargo. Only a few hundred have been made: rare, expensive and unproven. Its weakness is being top-heavy - the weapon clusters, missiles and sensor cluster all sit above the chest like a giant collar, which makes running, leaping and quick hand to hand awkward, and limits peripheral vision to about 90 degrees if the sensors go. A Northern Gun specialty, popular where Juicers and Crazies are outlawed or a serious problem, and in direct competition with the Defender - a stolen Northern Gun design the Black Market now produces. Juicer Uprising p.77-79.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.77-88'),
('bm-japeii-defender-exoskeleton', 'BM-JAPEII "Defender" Exoskeleton', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 800.0, 1100000, 'Black market 1.1 million credits for a new, fully powered suit', 'A high-powered STUN BLASTER with lethal and non-lethal settings, grenade launchers that take stun and riot control grenades as readily as lethal ones, and variable frequency lasers.', 1, 'Running 120 mph (192 kmph) maximum, tiring the operator at a fraction of the usual rate', 'Nuclear, with an average life of up to 10 years', 210, 'Model Type BM-JAPEII. Class: Urban Assault & Capture Exoskeleton. Crew: one. Northern Gun shelved the J.A.P.E. project for lack of interest and turned to deadlier armor like the JK1A and B. A decade later the Black Market took the plans in a raid on Northern Gun R&D, saw the potential with a few modifications, and has spent six years selling the J.A.P.E. II - commonly called the DEFENDER - in urban centres across North America. Its range of non-lethal to lethal systems makes it desirable to the more humane law-enforcement agencies: Lazlo has bought several dozen, as have Laramy and Kingsdale. By exactly the same token, slavers and other criminals use it to kidnap people on the stunner''s non-lethal setting. Main body 210 M.D.C. Height 8 feet (2.7 m), length 4 feet (1.2 m). Weight 800 lbs (360 kg) without ammunition or rifle, 1,400 lbs (630 kg) with. Physical strength equal to P.S. 30. No cargo. Juicer Uprising p.79-80.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.77-88'),
('tarantula-jump-bike', 'Tarantula Jump Bike', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 1545.0, 80000, 'Market cost 80,000 credits', 'Weapon systems are optional on this model; see the Piloting: Jump Bike Combat skill for the Bike Jump Attack, which does 3D6 M.D. on a successful landing.', 1, 'Top speed 200 mph (320 kmph), or 150 mph (240 kmph) on the alternative fuel setting. Cruising speed 100 mph (160 kmph). Range 500 miles (800 km), twelve hours of continuous operation.', 'Flex-fuel internal combustion with electric assist; the jump thrusters run on CNG from a separate tank holding five jumps', 100, 'Model Type: high performance motorcycle. Crew: one. Built for the physically enhanced customer - a niche that opened over the last decade because augmented humans like the Juicer and the Crazy found standard vehicles painfully sluggish. THE JUMP SYSTEM is the point: jumping distance is the current speed in miles per hour TRIPLED, in yards, and jump height is the speed in inches doubled. Anti-lock braking, traction control, active aerodynamics, solid rubber tires and a fully active suspension that reads the surface ahead and adjusts ride height and firmness by itself. Comes with an armored interface helmet wired to the bike by fiber optics, giving every benefit of a Juicer optics helmet plus a heads-up display of the bike''s vitals including remaining jump fuel and E-Clip status. Main body 100 M.D.C. Height 4 feet 1 inch (1.2 m), length 8 feet 7 inches (2.6 m). This is the bike the Piloting: Jump Bike Combat skill exists for. Juicer Uprising p.81-82.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.77-88'),
('road-boss-motorcycle', 'Road Boss', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 1850.0, 90000, 'Market cost 200,000 credits with full weapon systems, or 90,000 credits without them', 'A "Catapult" cannon (75 M.D.C.) among the full weapon package.', 1, 'Top speed 185 mph (296 kmph). Range 725 miles (1,160 km).', 'Flex-fuel internal combustion', 200, 'Model Type: motorcycle. Crew: one. The Road Boss is full-featured: anti-lock brakes, traction control, active suspension and high-density solid rubber tires, plus a custom set of interface goggles or sunglasses that give every benefit of the Tarantula''s interface helmet WITHOUT the head protection. Main body 200 M.D.C., wheels 30 each, "Catapult" cannon 75. Height 3 feet 10 inches (1.2 m), length 16 feet (4.9 m). The stored cost is the unarmed price, since the weapon systems are the option rather than the vehicle. Juicer Uprising p.83.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.77-88'),
('rolling-thunder-apv', '"Rolling Thunder" All-Purpose Vehicle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 2875.0, 275000, 'Black market 275,000 credits; manufactured by Wellington Industries', 'A radio-detonated plasma mine dispenser carrying twelve NG anti-vehicle mines, four of each grade - light 6D6 M.D. to a 30 foot (9.1 m) area, medium 1D6x10 M.D. to the same, heavy 3D4x10 M.D. to a 70 foot (21.3 m) area. One per melee round; the radio transmitter reaches about 3,000 feet (914 m). Mines cost 400, 600 and 1,000 credits respectively.', 1, 'Top speed 166 mph (265 kmph), or 142 mph (227 kmph) on the alternative setting', 'Flex-fuel internal combustion with electric back-up; twelve mines total', 155, 'Model Type: APV. Crew: one pilot and three passengers in comfort. A four-wheeled open-cockpit vehicle equally at home on and off the road, carrying most of the standard equipment of the two motorcycles plus extras. Its variable suspension is fully active and adjusts from 4 to 24 inches of ground clearance for bad terrain - though above six inches (0.15 m) the skill bonuses are negated, because the centre of gravity rises with it. Anti-lock brakes, traction control, solid rubber tires and a flex-fuel powerplant. THE MINE DISPENSER is the interesting system: mines can be dropped and radio-detonated on command, with a safety that will not let one go off within range of the Rolling Thunder itself, so pursuers must break off and lose ground. They can also be set to trigger when a target comes within 30-70 feet (9.1 to 21.3 m), which lets the crew string an ambush along a road. Main body 155 M.D.C. Height 5 feet 6 inches (1.65 m), length 20 feet (6.1 m). Juicer Uprising p.84-85.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.77-88'),
('ahb-2000-assault-hover-bike', 'AHB-2000 Assault Hover Bike (W.I.)', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 800.0, 900000, 'Market cost 900,000 credits for a new, undamaged, fully equipped AHB-2000', 'Particle beam guns (2), mounted over and under in the nose, plus the rest of an attack helicopter''s firepower in a one-man frame.', 1, 'Cannot drive on the ground. Hovers stationary up to 1,000 feet (305 m). Maximum flying speed 300 mph (480 kmph), cruising 100 to 200 mph (160 to 320 kmph), maximum altitude about 5,000 feet (1,524 m).', 'Nuclear; average energy life 10 years. The hover jets need to cool after twelve hours above cruising speed or twenty-four at cruising; with short rests at cruising speed it can fly almost indefinitely.', 190, 'Model Type AHB-2000. Class: Light Combat Hoverbike. Crew: one. Wellington Industries'' answer to Northern Gun''s Sky King: slower, with a lower ceiling - 5,000 feet against the Sky King''s 10,000 - but MORE HEAVILY ARMED AND ARMORED, with the firepower of an attack helicopter in a compact one-man vehicle. Fairly popular with mercenaries and independent kingdoms since it appeared. Main body 190 M.D.C. Height 4 feet (1.2 m), width 6 feet (1.8 m) counting the side weapon pods, length 9 feet (2.7 m). Weight 800 lbs (360 kg) fully loaded. Cargo is a small pilot''s compartment, big enough for a hand weapon and a few possessions. Juicer Uprising p.85-86.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.77-88'),
('ips-1-icarus-flight-system', 'IPS-1 Icarus Flight System', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 1000.0, 3200000, 'Market cost 3.2 million credits. Fair to poor availability, and the CS has OUTLAWED it.', 'High-powered laser guns (2) mounted on the front end, rotating through a 90 degree arc.', 1, 'Cannot drive on the ground. Flies at up to MACH ONE - 670 mph (1,078 kmph).', 'Nuclear; average energy life five years, though the jets themselves are the limit on endurance', 120, 'Model Type IPS-1. Class: Combat Flight System. Crew: one. A jet pack with the performance of a fighter, and ONLY A JUICER, BORG OR D-BEE WITH SUPERHUMAN STRENGTH AND ENDURANCE CAN SURVIVE THE G-FORCES IT GENERATES - which is also why it weighs 1,000 lbs (450 kg) and needs that strength simply to carry. It can be worn, or flown by REMOTE CONTROL: an experienced pilot can direct it from the ground and order it to attack designated targets. It attaches to the pilot''s armor by a magnetic seal and detaches in seconds, counting as one melee action - Juicer pilots often send the IPS up first and jump to connect with the wings in mid-air, purely to show off. Disassembled, the modular vehicle fits in the bed of a pickup or on the roof of a jeep, which lets a lightly equipped group of adventurers field a jet fighter with no hangar and no heavy transport. Main body 120 M.D.C. Height 5 feet (1.5 m), length 4 feet (1.2 m). No cargo. THE ICARUS BECOMES THE CORE OF THE JUICERS'' AIR FORCE DURING THE UPRISING, and the Piloting: Flight System Combat skill exists for it. Juicer Uprising p.86-88.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.77-88')
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS juicer_uprising_gear_c FROM gear WHERE source_book = 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.77-88';
SELECT slug, name, cost, mdc FROM gear
 WHERE slug IN ('ng-jk1-juicer-killer-power-armor', 'tarantula-jump-bike', 'road-boss-motorcycle',
                'ips-1-icarus-flight-system')
 ORDER BY slug;

-- Records this run. One row per run rather than per file: every statement above
-- guards itself, so this script is safe to re-run and safe to run early.
-- See db/migrations/024-data-script-runs.sql.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-juicer-uprising-gear-c.sql');
